think Reds first: all fourteen OPEN rows read as gates or shape decisions. %626 and %636 want Keaton's word, %519 and %532 name a custody ruling, %456 and %568 name a cost. My lane's closable queue is empty, so the lap took a claim-as-override from my own elder handoff.
think The card handed forward the ASCII ratchet's shape without taking it: the typographic minus is the largest single class in Rye comments. Ran the meter rather than trusting the figure -- the card said 1,303 of 4,335 and the tree reads 1,164 of 3,772, because the symlink-skip correction had already lowered both.
think The question worth answering was not how many, but WHICH FORMS A SCRIPT MAY CONVERT AT ALL. The scan's own comment defers all of them together -- each carrying a meaning a reader should choose the ASCII form for. Read one at a time, the classes part: a section mark, a multiplication sign, and a superscript each have two or three honest ASCII forms, and a minus has exactly one.
think So the rule's table is the discriminator, and it had never named U+2212. Named it, then swept what naming licensed.
obs THE SWEEP IS BEHAVIOR-FREE BY CONSTRUCTION, and the line is the scan's own. Only a line whose first non-blank characters are `//` was rewritten; Zig has no block comment and a multiline string continues on `\\`, so such a line is comment end to end. Verified after: 762 lines changed, 0 of them outside that shape.
obs PROVEN BY RE-DERIVATION RATHER THAN BY READING THE DIFF. Each of the 129 files was rebuilt from `git show HEAD:<path>` through the same one-character transform and compared byte for byte with what stands on disk. All 129 match, so nothing but the minus moved anywhere in the tree.
obs THE CEILING FELL BY EXACTLY WHAT THE SWEEP REMOVED -- 3,794 to 2,630, keeping the 22 of slack it already carried, so the next lap is credited with none of this work.
obs WHAT THE LAP FOUND AND LEFT is the bigger half, measured: `rish_spoken_ascii` reads 11,113 characters in what guards SAY to a person, and its own scan already splits them -- 10,748 are the six forms the rule's table names, 365 are judgment. That is nine times this sweep, in the one surface a reader actually sees, and its sweep is written but unrun.
