obs AGAINST MYSELF, TWICE. The hot pass reddened three guards on one cause -- the elder link inside my new shelf kept the pin's depth, the fault my own elder block recorded being caught by this same guard. `fold_shelf_link_repoint.sh --apply` made the repair the scan had already computed, and the cost was a second full hot pass rather than a second diagnosis. And I wrote one measurement to `/tmp` before switching to `.lap/`, which is the family the baton names three times.
obs THE REBASE BROUGHT TWO REDS THAT WERE NOT MINE, AND BOTH HAD A MECHANICAL CLOSE. A peer's shelf `construction/archive/20260909-000500_itinerary-landed-accounts.md` kept the pin's depth in its elder link -- the same fault my own shelf carried an hour earlier, which is a lantern firing twice in one lap from two hands. `fold_shelf_link_repoint.sh --apply` computed and made both repairs. And the day turned mid-lap: `log_has_a_row` read `pin_shelf_missing`, so `session-logs/README.md` gained the `20260909` open row and closed `20260908` at its 159 counted rows.
